IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `cpp-core`
IMPORT `cpp-core-calendar`

-- Canada Pension Plan Act, section 2(1) -- THE DEFINITIONS that can be worked out from facts.
--
-- Section 2(1) has 61 entries (63 terms: two entries define two terms each). Most of them only point to the section that does the work ("has the
-- meaning assigned by section 17"); those are listed in NOTES.md, "Defined terms", with the piece
-- that encodes the section they point to, and they have no rule here. This module holds the entries
-- that say something a rule can compute: applicant, balance-due day, beneficiary, benefit, business,
-- common-law partner, contribution, contributor, employee, employer, employment, office and officer,
-- pension, prescribed, representative, Social Insurance Number, the three kinds of contribution,
-- unadjusted pensionable earnings and year.
--
-- Where a definition turns on a fact the Act decides elsewhere (a contract of service, a division of
-- earnings approved under section 55.1, the earnings of subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i)), that fact is a plain
-- input here, named as the provision names it. The piece that encodes the other provision supplies it.
-- Where a definition says "includes", the rule is the union of the base meaning and the inclusions.

§ `Section 2(1) -- definitions`

§§ `Persons: applicant, beneficiary, contributor, representative`

-- src:17 | applicant means, in Part II,
-- src:18 | (a) a person or an estate that has applied for a benefit,
-- src:19 | (b) a person who has applied for a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings under section 55 or paragraph 55.1(1)(b) or (c), or
-- src:20 | (c) a person in respect of whom a division of unadjusted pensionable earnings has been approved under paragraph 55.1(1)(a); (requérant)
@ref Act s 2(1) "applicant" (src:17-20)
GIVEN `applied for a benefit` IS A BOOLEAN
      `applied for a division` IS A BOOLEAN
      `division approved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — an applicant, in Part II` `applied for a benefit` `applied for a division` `division approved` MEANS
    `applied for a benefit` OR `applied for a division` OR `division approved`

-- src:28 | beneficiary means a person, estate or other body to whom a benefit has become payable; (bénéficiaire)
@ref Act s 2(1) "beneficiary" (src:28)
GIVEN `a benefit has become payable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a beneficiary` `a benefit has become payable` MEANS
    `a benefit has become payable`

-- src:35 | contributor means a person who has made an employee’s contribution or a contribution in respect of the person’s self-employed earnings, and includes a person the amount of whose earnings on which a contribution has been made for a year under this Act calculated as provided in subparagraph 53(1)(b)(i) exceeds zero and a person to whom unadjusted pensionable earnings have been attributed under section 55, 55.1 or 55.2; (cotisant)
@ref Act s 2(1) "contributor" (src:35)
GIVEN `made an employee's contribution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `made a contribution on own self-employed earnings` IS A BOOLEAN
      `earnings contributed on, per year, as in 53(1)(b)(i)`
          IS A LIST OF NUMBER
      `earnings attributed under 55, 55.1 or 55.2` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a contributor` `made an employee's contribution` `made a contribution on own self-employed earnings` `earnings contributed on, per year, as in 53(1)(b)(i)` `earnings attributed under 55, 55.1 or 55.2` MEANS
    `made an employee's contribution` OR `made a contribution on own self-employed earnings` OR (any (GIVEN amount YIELD amount GREATER THAN 0) `earnings contributed on, per year, as in 53(1)(b)(i)`) OR `earnings attributed under 55, 55.1 or 55.2`

-- src:61 | representative means, in respect of any person, a guardian, curator, committee, executor, liquidator of a succession, administrator or other legal representative of that person; (représentant)
@ref Act s 2(1) "representative" (src:61)
DECLARE `Kind of representative` IS ONE OF
    `a guardian`
    `a curator`
    `a committee`
    `an executor`
    `a liquidator of a succession`
    `an administrator`
    `another legal representative`
    `not a representative`

@ref Act s 2(1) "representative" (src:61)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of representative`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a representative of a person` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `not a representative` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

§§ `Employment: employee, employer, employment, office and officer, business`

-- src:43 | employment means the state of being employed under an express or implied contract of service or apprenticeship, and includes the tenure of an office; (emploi)
@ref Act s 2(1) "employment" (src:43)
GIVEN `employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the tenure of an office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — employment` `employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` `the tenure of an office` MEANS
    `employed under a contract of service or apprenticeship` OR `the tenure of an office`

-- src:52 | office means the position of an individual entitling him to a fixed or ascertainable stipend or remuneration and includes a judicial office, the office of a minister of the Crown, the office of a lieutenant governor, the office of a member of the Senate or House of Commons, a member of a legislative assembly or a member of a legislative or executive council and any other office the incumbent of which is elected by popular vote or is elected or appointed in a representative capacity, and also includes the position of a corporation director, and officer means a person holding such an office; (fonction ou charge et fonctionnaire)
@ref Act s 2(1) "office" (src:52)
DECLARE `Kind of position` IS ONE OF
    `a judicial office`
    `the office of a minister of the Crown`
    `the office of a lieutenant governor`
    `the office of a member of the Senate or House of Commons`
    `the office of a member of a legislative assembly`
    `the office of a member of a legislative or executive council`
    `an office whose incumbent is elected by popular vote`
    `an office whose incumbent is elected or appointed in a representative capacity`
    `the position of a corporation director`
    `another position`

@ref Act s 2(1) "office" (src:52)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of position`
      `entitles the holder to a fixed or ascertainable stipend or remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — an office` kind `entitles the holder to a fixed or ascertainable stipend or remuneration` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `another position` THEN `entitles the holder to a fixed or ascertainable stipend or remuneration`
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@ref Act s 2(1) "officer" (src:52)
GIVEN `holds the position` IS A BOOLEAN
      kind IS A `Kind of position`
      `entitles the holder to a fixed or ascertainable stipend or remuneration` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — an officer` `holds the position` kind `entitles the holder to a fixed or ascertainable stipend or remuneration` MEANS
    `holds the position` AND `s 2(1) — an office` kind `entitles the holder to a fixed or ascertainable stipend or remuneration`

-- src:41 | employee includes an officer; (employé)
@ref Act s 2(1) "employee" (src:41)
GIVEN `in employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — an employee` `in employment` `an officer` MEANS
    `in employment` OR `an officer`

-- src:42 | employer means a person liable to pay salary, wages or other remuneration in relation to employment, and, in relation to an officer, includes the person from whom the officer receives their remuneration; (employeur)
@ref Act s 2(1) "employer" (src:42)
GIVEN `liable to pay salary, wages or other remuneration in relation to employment` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other is an officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer receives their remuneration from the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — an employer` `liable to pay salary, wages or other remuneration in relation to employment` `the other is an officer` `the officer receives their remuneration from the person` MEANS
    `liable to pay salary, wages or other remuneration in relation to employment` OR (`the other is an officer` AND `the officer receives their remuneration from the person`)

-- src:30 | business includes a profession, calling, trade, manufacture or undertaking of any kind whatever, and includes an adventure or concern in the nature of trade but does not include an office or employment; (entreprise)
@ref Act s 2(1) "business" (src:30)
DECLARE `Kind of activity` IS ONE OF
    `a profession`
    `a calling`
    `a trade`
    `a manufacture`
    `an undertaking of any kind whatever`
    `an adventure or concern in the nature of trade`
    `an office`
    `an employment`
    `another activity`

@ref Act s 2(1) "business" (src:30)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of activity`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a business` kind MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `an office` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `an employment` THEN JUST FALSE
    WHEN `another activity` THEN NOTHING
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Benefits, pensions and contributions`

-- src:29 | benefit means a benefit payable under this Act and includes a pension; (prestation)
@ref Act s 2(1) "benefit" (src:29)
GIVEN `payable under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a benefit` `payable under this Act` MEANS
    `payable under this Act`

-- src:53 | pension means a pension payable under this Act; (pension)
@ref Act s 2(1) "pension" (src:53)
GIVEN `pension payable under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a pension` `pension payable under this Act` MEANS
    `pension payable under this Act`

-- src:33 | contribution means a contribution under this Act; (cotisation)
@ref Act s 2(1) "contribution" (src:33)
GIVEN `a contribution under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a contribution` `a contribution under this Act` MEANS
    `a contribution under this Act`

-- src:25 | base contribution means a contribution under subsection 8(1), 9(1) or 10(1); (cotisation de base)
-- src:45 | first additional contribution means a contribution under subsection 8(1.1), 9(1.1) or 10(1.1); (première cotisation supplémentaire)
-- src:67 | second additional contribution means a contribution under subsection 8(1.2), 9(1.2) or 10(1.2); (deuxième cotisation supplémentaire)
@ref Act s 2(1) "base contribution", "first additional contribution", "second additional contribution" (src:25-67)
GIVEN subsection IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE Tier
`s 2(1) — the tier of a contribution made under a subsection` subsection MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF subsection EQUALS "8(1)" OR subsection EQUALS "9(1)" OR subsection EQUALS "10(1)" THEN JUST `the base tier`
        IF subsection EQUALS "8(1.1)" OR subsection EQUALS "9(1.1)" OR subsection EQUALS "10(1.1)" THEN JUST `the first additional tier`
        IF subsection EQUALS "8(1.2)" OR subsection EQUALS "9(1.2)" OR subsection EQUALS "10(1.2)" THEN JUST `the second additional tier`
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

@ref Act s 2(1) "base contribution", "first additional contribution", "second additional contribution" (src:25-67)
GIVEN tier IS A Tier
      capacity IS A `Contributing capacity`
GIVETH A STRING
`s 2(1) — the subsection that imposes a contribution of a tier and capacity` tier capacity MEANS
    CONSIDER capacity
    WHEN `contributing as an employee` THEN `s 2(1) — the subsection of section 8 for a tier` tier
    WHEN `contributing as an employer` THEN `s 2(1) — the subsection of section 9 for a tier` tier
    WHEN `contributing as a self-employed person` THEN `s 2(1) — the subsection of section 10 for a tier` tier

-- The three subsections of each of sections 8, 9 and 10, one per tier.
@ref Act s 2(1) "base contribution", "first additional contribution", "second additional contribution" (src:25-67)
GIVEN tier IS A Tier
GIVETH A STRING
`s 2(1) — the subsection of section 8 for a tier` tier MEANS
    CONSIDER tier
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN "8(1)"
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN "8(1.1)"
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN "8(1.2)"

@ref Act s 2(1) "base contribution", "first additional contribution", "second additional contribution" (src:25-67)
GIVEN tier IS A Tier
GIVETH A STRING
`s 2(1) — the subsection of section 9 for a tier` tier MEANS
    CONSIDER tier
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN "9(1)"
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN "9(1.1)"
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN "9(1.2)"

@ref Act s 2(1) "base contribution", "first additional contribution", "second additional contribution" (src:25-67)
GIVEN tier IS A Tier
GIVETH A STRING
`s 2(1) — the subsection of section 10 for a tier` tier MEANS
    CONSIDER tier
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN "10(1)"
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN "10(1.1)"
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN "10(1.2)"

-- src:79 | unadjusted pensionable earnings means base unadjusted pensionable earnings, first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings and second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings; (gains non ajustés ouvrant droit à pension)
@ref Act s 2(1) "unadjusted pensionable earnings" (src:79)
GIVEN earnings IS A `Unadjusted pensionable earnings`
      tier IS A Tier
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) — the unadjusted pensionable earnings of a tier` earnings tier MEANS
    CONSIDER tier
    WHEN `the base tier` THEN earnings's `base unadjusted pensionable earnings`
    WHEN `the first additional tier` THEN earnings's `first additional unadjusted pensionable earnings`
    WHEN `the second additional tier` THEN earnings's `second additional unadjusted pensionable earnings`

§§ `Dates, the calendar year, and the common-law partner`

-- src:80 | year means a calendar year; (année)
@ref Act s 2(1) "year" (src:80)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2(1) — the year that contains a date` d MEANS DATE_YEAR d

@ref Act s 2(1) "year" (src:80)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2(1) — the first day of a year` year MEANS YMD year 1 1

@ref Act s 2(1) "year" (src:80)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2(1) — the last day of a year` year MEANS YMD year 12 31

-- src:22 | balance-due day of a person for a year means
-- src:23 | (a) where the person died after October in the year and before May in the immediately following year, the day that is 6 months after the day of death, and
-- src:24 | (b) in any other case, April 30 in the immediately following year; (date d’exigibilité du solde)
@ref Act s 2(1) "balance-due day" (src:22-24)
GIVEN year IS A NUMBER
      `date of death` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 2(1) — the balance-due day of a person for a year` year `date of death` MEANS
    CONSIDER `date of death`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `April 30 in the immediately following year`
    WHEN JUST died THEN
        IF died AT LEAST (YMD year 11 1) AND died AT MOST (YMD (year PLUS 1) 4 30)
        THEN `the date a time limit ends` died (`a number of months` WITH `number of months` IS 6)
        ELSE `April 30 in the immediately following year`
    WHERE
        `April 30 in the immediately following year` MEANS YMD (year PLUS 1) 4 30

-- src:31 | common-law partner, in relation to a contributor, means a person who is cohabiting with the contributor in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time, having so cohabited with the contributor for a continuous period of at least one year. For greater certainty, in the case of a contributor’s death, the relevant time means the time of the contributor’s death; (conjoint de fait)
@ref Act s 2(1) "common-law partner" (src:31)
GIVEN `cohabiting in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` IS A BOOLEAN
      `day the continuous cohabitation began` IS A DATE
      `the relevant time` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a common-law partner of a contributor at a relevant time` `cohabiting in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` `day the continuous cohabitation began` `the relevant time` MEANS
    `cohabiting in a conjugal relationship at the relevant time` AND `the relevant time` AT LEAST (`the date a time limit ends` `day the continuous cohabitation began` (`a number of years` WITH `number of years` IS 1))

-- The "for greater certainty" sentence: for a contributor's death the relevant time is the date of death.
@ref Act s 2(1) "common-law partner" (src:31)
GIVEN `cohabiting in a conjugal relationship at the death` IS A BOOLEAN
      `day the continuous cohabitation began` IS A DATE
      `date of the death` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a common-law partner of a contributor at the contributor's death` `cohabiting in a conjugal relationship at the death` `day the continuous cohabitation began` `date of the death` MEANS
    `s 2(1) — a common-law partner of a contributor at a relevant time` `cohabiting in a conjugal relationship at the death` `day the continuous cohabitation began` `date of the death`

§§ `Prescribed`

-- src:57 | prescribed means
-- src:58 | (a) in the case of a form or the information to be given on a form, authorized by the Minister having the control and direction of the administration of the Part of this Act to which the context extends, and
-- src:59 | (b) in any other case, prescribed by regulation or determined in accordance with rules prescribed by regulation; (prescrit)
@ref Act s 2(1) "prescribed" (src:57-59)
DECLARE `Kind of matter that may be prescribed` IS ONE OF
    `a form or the information to be given on a form`
    `any other matter`

@ref Act s 2(1) "prescribed" (src:57-59)
GIVEN kind IS A `Kind of matter that may be prescribed`
      `authorized by the Minister administering the Part` IS A BOOLEAN
      `prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `determined by rules prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — prescribed` kind `authorized by the Minister administering the Part` `prescribed by regulation` `determined by rules prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `a form or the information to be given on a form` THEN `authorized by the Minister administering the Part`
    WHEN `any other matter` THEN `prescribed by regulation` OR `determined by rules prescribed by regulation`

§§ `Social Insurance Number`

-- src:73 | Social Insurance Number means a Social Insurance Number assigned to an individual under the authority of any Act of Parliament, and Social Insurance Number Card means a Social Insurance Number Card issued to an individual under that authority; (numéro d’assurance sociale et carte matricule d’assurance sociale)
@ref Act s 2(1) "Social Insurance Number" (src:73)
GIVEN `assigned under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a Social Insurance Number` `assigned under an Act of Parliament` MEANS
    `assigned under an Act of Parliament`

@ref Act s 2(1) "Social Insurance Number Card" (src:73)
GIVEN `issued under an Act of Parliament` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 2(1) — a Social Insurance Number Card` `issued under an Act of Parliament` MEANS
    `issued under an Act of Parliament`
